    <string name="badge_info_title">CPU governor</string>
    <string name="badge_info_what">"Takeover" means this module switches each CPU policy's scaling_governor to userspace and publishes a target frequency every cycle. Without it the platform's own governor (schedutil here) picks frequencies.</string>
    <string name="badge_info_off">Right now the governor is untouched, which is the default: on this device scaling_max_freq is read-only at the driver level, so tuning can only happen through full userspace takeover — more risk than benefit unless it is asked for explicitly with UPERF_CPU_GOVERNOR=1.</string>
    <string name="badge_info_on">Right now the governor is taken over. If the daemon stops or is killed, the watchdog restores the value recorded before takeover.</string>
